From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:33:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: answer the DCP's PMU temperature query

At start the internal DCP's backlight compensation asks the AP for the
PMU temperature: D401, object "SUMP", key "Temperature". The v14.7 and
H17P paths answer it with the battery temperature in 0.1 K. The M4 path
sends every D401 to its property store, where nothing ever stores this
key, so the firmware logs "set_PMU_service: failed to read PMU
temperature property!" on the J604's mini-LED panel. macOS's log of the
same machine has no such line.

Answer it on the M4 path the same way, before the property store.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 149be02275..9aa1a5ea9c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1735,7 +1735,24 @@ static int dcp_m4_runtime_property(void *cookie, unsigned int method,
 				    const void *input, void *output)
 {
 	struct dcp_m4_runtime *r = cookie;
-	int ret = dcp_m4_property_callback(r->properties, method, input, output);
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The PMU temperature, the battery temperature in 0.1 K, as the v14.7
+	 * and H17P paths answer it. The panel's backlight compensation reads it
+	 * at start ("set_PMU_service"); no AP property ever stores it, so the
+	 * property store below would answer "not found".
+	 */
+	if (method == 401 && !memcmp(input, "SUMP", 4) &&
+	    !strncmp((const char *)input + 4, "Temperature", 64)) {
+		u8 *out = output;
+
+		put_unaligned_le64(dcp_pmu_temperature(r->dcp->dev), out);
+		out[8] = 1;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	ret = dcp_m4_property_callback(r->properties, method, input, output);
 
 	if (!ret && r->dcp->external)
 		dcp_m4_ext_property(r, method, input);
-- 
